# Design System with @theme and OKLCH

## Overview
Tailwind CSS v4 uses `@theme` to define design tokens. Use OKLCH for perceptually uniform colors.

## Tokens

```css
@theme {
  /* Color */
  --color-brand-50: oklch(0.98 0.02 250);
  --color-brand-500: oklch(0.65 0.18 250);
  --color-brand-950: oklch(0.20 0.08 250);

  /* Spacing scale */
  --spacing: 0.25rem;

  /* Radius */
  --radius-sm: 0.375rem;
  --radius-md: 0.5rem;
  --radius-lg: 0.75rem;

  /* Shadows */
  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px oklch(0 0 0 / 0.05);
  --shadow-lg: 0 10px 15px oklch(0 0 0 / 0.10);

  /* Font */
  --font-sans: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: ui-monospace, monospace;
}
```

## Best Practices

- Define semantic tokens, not raw values
- Use OKLCH for color harmony and accessibility
- Keep scales consistent: spacing, radius, typography
- Export tokens for JS via CSS variables when needed
- Avoid hard-coded colors in components

## Usage

```css
.btn {
  background: var(--color-brand-500);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: calc(var(--spacing) * 3) calc(var(--spacing) * 4);
}
```
